#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0231 expect=noViolation domain=ADSL
#note "The OTHER direction of the mixed-group mechanic, and it does NOT skip: TRT01P, the operator's KEY, is absent. TR01PG1 seeds tuple (xx=01, y=1) and TRTxxP is synthesised by concreteFromTuple as the absent column TRT01P, so the rule executes: var_exists(\"TRT01P\") is false and not empty(TRT01P) is broadcast false, and the verdict is a silent no-violation even though the degraded key would collapse the table into one group and flag row 3."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
dataset ADSL
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col TR01PG1 type=Char
---
S1 | 001 | POOLX
S1 | 002 | POOLX
S1 | 003 | POOLY
